      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALLMIGHTY MAX (1) found some form last start when he found the lead and did well to go on and score by a head at Redcliffe over 1780m. No excuses from this advantageous draw. Stepping up a level this time but he is capable of making it consecutive wins. CAMERINA (10) led last start and saluted in a far better performance at this track over 1660m, getting home by 1.5 metres. Hard to know where she gets from this slightly awkward draw. Recent effort is good enough to put her right in the finish. BART BENTLEY (7) won two starts ago then things went wrong last start when he copped interference then broke and finished 14 metres away in 12th over 2138m at this track. Must overcome another very wide draw. Only needs to get some luck to be in the money. LOSTANDFOUND (8) is worth another chance after a last-start seventh over 2040m at Redcliffe two-and-a-half weeks ago.",
